-- The limit of naming a default's owner behind its heading (overnight card O6,
-- 2026-10-11): a rule declared at the top of a file has no heading to name, and
-- a call cannot say which file's `scaled` it means, so two imported files that
-- each declare one give a single entry. The rows answer 30, 50 and 80, and
-- every one lists `WITH scaled: rate`.

IMPORT `batch-typically-collide-import-a`
IMPORT `batch-typically-collide-import-b`

@export default Combine
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      one IS A BOOLEAN
      two IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS (IF one THEN useOne n ELSE 0) PLUS (IF two THEN useTwo n ELSE 0)
